Dogs and cats are carnivorous, so only eat meat.  Lichens are
plant matter, so they won't eat it, even if it is safe for you.

One role gets a pony for a pet; a pony won't eat the dead
animals, but will gobble down lichens (and other safe plant
corpses).

> with a ration i found he was first reluctent to go near it but
> later picked it up for a bit then dropped it, that a bad sign?

If he picked it up, no.  Human food isn't a corpse, and your pet
will only eat it if it is really hungry.

> cause he never ate it, also can the same tactic work to find
> out if armor is cursed?

If your pet walks over something, with no particular reason
(i.e. no food on it, you didn't displace him on it, etc.), and
no complains, it's not cursed.  This is mostly useful for trying
out armor early on, and to a lesser degree, weapons.

